A||||7||Fierokid87||removing CV joints||||4||
Z||000000||Fierokid87||07-18-2001||12:46 PM||||Ok all here is the situation.  Im trying to remove the CV joints on my engine cradle so I can used them as a core charge for reman. ones.  But the problem is  I dont have a tranny or an engine attached to them.  How do you keep them from spinning?<P>Scott<P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="BLOODY"> Fierokid's  Web site<BR>http://www.angelfire.com/sports/sfiero<P>AIM: Fierokid87<BR>ICQ: Fierokid</FONT><P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sfiero.JPG"> ||||reg||4
Z||000001||Steve Normington||07-18-2001||12:50 PM||||I assume you are trying to remove the hub nut. If you have an impact wrench, you can have someone hold the shaft (with work gloves) while the impact wrench takes off the nut. You might be able to rent an electrical wrench if you don't have air tools. The other method would be to jam a 3/8 ratchet extension through one of the holes in the hub and turn the nut until the extension buts up against the caliper mounting (with the caliper removed).||||reg||1
Z||000002||starfighter007@msn.com||07-18-2001||12:51 PM||||try useing a pipe wrench to hold the axle||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fierokid87||07-18-2001||12:53 PM||||Can you pleas e show me what your talking about so I dont mess something up.  <BR>And how heavy is the cradle with the struts and springs on there?  Cuzz I would have to carry the cradle to the barn where the air tank is.<P><BR>Scott<P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="BLOODY"> Fierokid's  Web site<BR>http://www.angelfire.com/sports/sfiero<P>AIM: Fierokid87<BR>ICQ: Fierokid</FONT><P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sfiero.JPG"> ||||reg||4
Z||000004||AutoXer||07-18-2001||01:10 PM||||I am pretty sure that the pipe wrench on the axle won't work.  The axle is pretty hard steel.<P>I would put a pipe or a large bar between the lug bolts and let it hit the ground.<P>Good luck.  That axle nut is very tight.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Carrolles||07-18-2001||01:47 PM||||How about bolting the rim back onto the hub to give you something to grab while you wrench on the axel nut?||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||07-18-2001||07:19 PM||||Put any junk wheel on and put the car's weight on it. Block the wheel if the car tries to move. The nut will come off easily this way.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Fierokid87||07-19-2001||03:17 AM||||Hmmm.  I like the wheel idea.  Maybe Ill try that.<P>Scott<P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="BLOODY"> Fierokid's  Web site<BR>http://www.angelfire.com/sports/sfiero<P>AIM: Fierokid87<BR>ICQ: Fierokid</FONT><P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sfiero.JPG"> ||||reg||10
